# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# Hash-pinned PowerShell scripts MUST check out with LF on every platform.
#
# With `text=auto` alone these were stored LF and checked out CRLF on
# Windows, so the SHA-256 on disk never matched the SHA-256 in the committed
# manifest — and apps/agent-node/src/exec/executor.ts refuses any script
# whose disk hash doesn't match. The effect was that every signed playbook
# was rejected on every Windows agent, which is every agent.
#
# The executor and generate-manifests.ts also normalize line endings before
# hashing, so a stray CRLF from an editor can't break execution either. This
# line makes the checkout deterministic; that normalization makes it robust.
*.ps1 text eol=lf
